## Proposal 3 — test layout / counts

The unit and cross-validation suites grew. The full test count moved
from **56** at the end of the v1 build session to **66** at the end of
the v1.1 hardening pass.

**Current** (`CLAUDE.md` ## Tooling > Tests):

```
- **Tests:**
  - `tests/unit/` — runs in CI. Uses a hand-built ~1M-param toy
    transformer (defined in `tests/fixtures/tiny_transformer.py`).
    Tests math correctness (Hutchinson convergence to exact trace
    as `n → ∞`, `χ_loss` closed-form vs autograd ground truth, `δL`
    symmetry, normalization invariants).
```

**Proposed**: bullet by bullet:

- Update the `tests/unit/` description to reflect the v1.1 additions:

  ```
  - `tests/unit/` — runs in CI. Uses a hand-built ~1M-param toy
    transformer (defined in `tests/fixtures/tiny_transformer.py`).
    Tests math correctness (Hutchinson convergence to exact trace
    as `n → ∞`, `χ_loss` closed-form correctness on the supported
    CE shapes, `δL` symmetry, normalization invariants). v1.1 added
    exact-NTK ground-truth tests for `chi_pos` and `delta_loss(A,B)`
    via an explicit per-token Jacobian builder
    (`_build_full_jacobian_and_u` in `tests/unit/test_chi_net.py`),
    plus a heavy-padding LM regression test against the same
    explicit-Jacobian reference, plus a `per_seq_cv` startup memory
    pre-check test.
  ```

  (Note: removed the `chi_loss closed-form vs autograd ground truth`
  bullet because v1.1 task 6 deleted `chi_loss_from_autograd`. The
  closed form is now validated against an explicit Jacobian instead.)

- Update the `tests/cross_validation/` description:

  ```
  - `tests/cross_validation/` — gated behind `pytest -m
    cross_validation`, **skipped in CI** (requires perspic in the
    environment), runnable locally. Cross-validates every observable
    against perspic as the ground-truth reference implementation. The
    protocol is unchanged; v1.1 added a tight-tolerance test
    (`test_all_observables_tight_tolerance_at_n16384`) at relative
    0.3% / absolute 1e-6 with `n_hutchinson = 16384`, plus a
    heavy-padding test (`test_heavy_padding_matches_perspic_on_valid_subset`)
    that drives 5/8 samples through `labels=-100` and asserts the
    padded vatis run agrees with perspic on the unpadded subset.
  ```

- Update the `tests/integration/` description: no change (no new
  integration tests in v1.1).

- Update the rolling test count line wherever it appears (the
  README at the top of `CLAUDE.md` doesn't list a count, so this
  is an additive note — propose adding it once to `tests/` heading):

  ```
  Test counts at the end of v1.1: 49 unit tests + 14 cross-validation
  tests + 4 integration tests = 67 total. CI runs 49 (unit only).
  ```

  (49 = 42 v1 unit tests − 3 (task 6 deleted `chi_loss_from_autograd`
  tests) + 5 (task 7 memory tests) + 2 (task 2 exact-NTK tests) +
  1 (task 4 LM padding test) + 1 (task 5 cross-pair contract test) +
  1 (task 1 revision-threading test). 14 = 10 v1 cross-validation tests
  + 2 (task 3 tight-tolerance, parametrized over both vatis methods)
  + 2 (task 4 heavy padding, parametrized over both vatis methods).
  The exact split is in `git log --oneline`.)

**Rationale**: the existing description references the
`chi_loss_from_autograd` ground truth, which v1.1 deleted (task 6).
Updating the bullet keeps the doc honest about what the unit suite
actually validates.

