## Notes the user might want to apply manually (out of scope for this proposal)

- The "Loss handling" section currently says non-CE losses fall back to
  `torch.autograd.grad(loss, logits)`. The v1.1 hardening pass deleted
  the helper that implemented this; the analyzer now only supports CE.
  I left this section alone because it isn't in the allowed-edit list,
  but it's mentioned in `FOLLOWUPS.md` for the user to handle.
- The "Implementation order" says to add `vatis/data/batches.py` in
  step 7, but in practice `data/collate.py` was needed earlier. The
  build session SESSION_SUMMARY.md already documents this; no need to
  update CLAUDE.md if the implementation order is purely descriptive
  of the past.
